Yes it can be worked around by using guard clauses, but it leads to more code that does the same thing and takes usefulness away from default values.
```
    func _init(thing, vars=null, calls=null):
        if vars == null:
            self.vars = {} # setting default value here
        if calls == null:
            self.calls = {} # setting default value here

        # setup ...
```
